Package: xt-wg-common
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 iptables,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends:
 xt-wg-dkms | xt-wg-source,
Description: xtables WireGuard helpers [userspace iptables plugins]
 Three xtables targets for running WireGuard across hostile or asymmetric
 networks, shipped together as a single consolidated xt_wg.ko kernel
 module plus three userspace iptables plugins:
 .
   * WGOBFS    - chacha-keyed payload obfuscation; DPI cannot fingerprint
                 the WireGuard message shape.
   * WGANYCAST - WG-protocol-aware dynamic anycast pool learning with
                 per-packet outbound spray.
   * WGPTCP    - UDP-to-fake-TCP transmutation with stateful tracking
                 via the kernel's conntrack accounting, so middleboxes
                 that block or rate-limit UDP let the flow through.
 .
 This package provides only the userspace iptables plugins
 (libxt_WGOBFS.so, libxt_WGANYCAST.so, libxt_WGPTCP.so).  The matching
 xt_wg.ko kernel module must be built and installed separately via the
 xt-wg-dkms or xt-wg-source package.

Package: xt-wg-source
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 bzip2,
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 module-assistant (>= 0.11.14~),
 ${misc:Depends},
Recommends:
 xt-wg-common (>= ${source:Version}),
Description: xtables WireGuard helpers [kernel module source for module-assistant]
 Source tarball of the xt_wg.ko kernel module, intended for use with
 module-assistant.  After installing this package, run
 .
   m-a a-i xt-wg
 .
 to compile and install a kernel-version-specific binary package named
 xt-wg-modules-$(uname -r).
 .
 Kernel headers (linux-headers-$(uname -r)) are required to compile.
 The xt-wg-common package is also required to use the resulting kernel
 module.

Package: xt-wg-dkms
Section: kernel
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 dkms,
 ${misc:Depends},
Recommends:
 xt-wg-common (>= ${source:Version}),
Description: xtables WireGuard helpers [kernel module source for DKMS]
 Source of the xt_wg.ko kernel module, managed by DKMS so that the
 module is automatically rebuilt for each kernel installed on the
 system.  No manual step is needed after install.
 .
 Kernel headers (linux-headers-$(uname -r)) must be available so DKMS
 can build the module.  The xt-wg-common package is also required to
 use the resulting kernel module.
